        "input": {
          "level": "fallback",
          "precedentId": "seed-govlaw",
          "summary": "Send unresolved Disputes to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Delaware state and federal courts and delete the now-redundant ICDR arbitration process.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] Delaware governing law is acceptable to us, but we cannot accept mandatory ICDR international arbitration as the merits forum; we have directed unresolved Disputes (including intellectual property ownership matters) to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Delaware state and federal courts that correspond to the chosen law, and deleted the arbitration process that is now redundant. The existing right to seek preliminary injunctive relief in any court of competent jurisdiction is preserved.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0824",
              "oldText": "then such Dispute shall be submitted to the International Centre for Dispute Resolution (\"ICDR\") for final and binding arbitration pursuant to the arbitration clause set forth in Section 15.10.2. Notwithstanding the foregoing, no matters relating to breach or alleged breach of the ownership of intellectual property or rights in intellectual property or the validity or enforceability thereof shall be resolved by arbitration, but rather shall be determined by a U.S. federal court of appropriate jurisdiction.",
              "newText": "then such Dispute, including any matter relating to breach or alleged breach of the ownership of intellectual property or rights in intellectual property or the validity or enforceability thereof, shall be brought exclusively in the state and federal courts located in the State of Delaware, and each Party irrevocably submits to the exclusive jurisdiction of such courts."
